    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for the Austin Waves today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who registers as our only \"Strong\" tier play above the 80.0 threshold. Facing Gray, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a dynamic platoon advantage that boosts his output potential to an 81.88, making him the cornerstone of our lineup. Following closely, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (68.14) and **Heliot Ramos** (62.21) provide essential support; **Heliot Ramos** is particularly intriguing against Ray, where the high xERA of 4.90 and a favorable lefty-righty dynamic overcome his neutral park factor to solidify his status as a must-start.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the day involved **Liam Hicks**, whose 39.70 score fell just short of our 40.0 floor. Despite a decent platoon edge against deGrom, the elite SP skill of the opposing arm ultimately suppressed his ceiling, leaving him on the bench behind **Dominic Smith**, whose historical BvP edge and park adjustment kept him just inside our playable range. We are exercising caution with **Kyle Tucker** (55.25) and **Jackson Merrill** (53.64); while both are high-ceiling assets, they face tough arms in Cavalli and Rod\u00f3n, respectively. Notably, **Miguel Vargas** remains in the lineup with a 50.34 score, largely due to his aggressive base-running potential against a slow pitcher delivery, a critical factor given our emphasis on maintaining momentum in the stolen base category. \n\nManagers should keep a close watch on **Drake Baldwin** (49.38) and **Sam Antonacci** (56.02), both of whom are facing the formidable Wheeler and Bradley. While their lead-off spots provide volume, their scores are susceptible to the high-strikeout nature of their opponents. We have successfully avoided the trap of starting marginal bench pieces like **Wade Meckler**, prioritizing our roster's daily efficiency caps to ensure we aren't burning game slots on sub-40 performers. Keep an eye on weather reports, as the pitching matchups for **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith** carry significant risk should late-day conditions deteriorate against Wheeler.",
